"prose": [
{
"from": 308,
"to": 319,
"text": "**The gates:** - a probe that no manifest or lock changed, measured from the base `739132d5f`, HEAD when P4 wrote it; - the `--locked` workspace build; - the two crates' unit tests; - the new target; - the edited declared-node target; - the companions that read the snapshot, the graph, actions, the lint, exploration, MCP, the spans, replay, the   cross-OS digests and the canvas; - the seven_guis process checks that read the help and refusal texts and the hosts' logs; - the `a11y` leg, whose result line step 15 states; - the pre-push gate (`fast`), which runs the CI-script tests among them; - the `doc` leg, because the chunk edits public doc comments."
},
{
"from": 321,
"to": 327,
"text": "**What is absent:** - There is no boot-path touchpoint (no binary's start changes) and no smoke entry. - There is no live leg, and no headful self-verify harness in this project. - There is no `audit` leg: the probe holds every manifest and the lock unchanged. - There is no `stand-repeat`. The new target is no `stand_` file, and its fixture is no stand task. - The coverage leg is not run locally. CI's coverage job reads the dioxus-native-dom (83 %) and escher-driver (97 %)   floors on the pushed tree, and the CI read asserts green over it."
},
{
"from": 329,
"to": 330,
"text": "**The controls** are step 16's one-shot runs. The diff adds one OS-conditional site, step 12's `#[cfg(unix)]` case, which the CI read names."
}
],
